                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1307-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_sc.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Supercardioid" title="Supercardioid" ></span>R&#00216;DE NTG-3</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Supercardioid Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>NTG-3 is a short shotgun microphone with a high sensitivity and supercardioid polar pattern. </p><p>The mic uses Rode&#8217;s RF Bias technology, making it resistant to temperature and humidity changes. </p><p>The NTG-3 has a wider, more forgiving polar pattern than other shotgun microphones, making it easier for booming.</p><blockquote><p><cite>ProVideo Coalition</cite><br />The mic has a slightly wider pick-up pattern than the [Sennheiser] 416 with a gentler transition to off-axis rejection. This design choice makes two-shots and moving characters easier to cover, but also means that in noisy locations you may pick up some unexpected and unwanted sound.</p></blockquote><p>The NTG-3 ships with a protective aluminum tube case, RM5 hard mount, foam windscreen, and a leather storage pouch.<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Rode/NTG-3">R&#00216;DE NTG-3</a> is also known as: NTG3.</p>
